  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Innovation for Affordable and Renewable Energy for All (INARA)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(Lebanon):  Using FY 2024 assistance, the Innovation for Affordable and Renewable Energy for All (INARA) activity will work with groups of communities to improve the availability and reliability of electricity supply in Lebanon, while reducing its costs to enterprise and non-business users alike. Toward this end, INARA will initiate solar energy solutions to benefit a cluster of villages in the Bekaa Valley. The activity will work on building private and public sector partnerships with clusters of communities and will also employ community energy NGOs to oversee and safeguard operation and maintenance of these systems in a transparent manner that builds trust in local government and foments civic engagement and education. INARA will also explore opportunities for addressing the needs of communities affected by fighting between Hizballah and Israel for the restoration of basic energy services.  These interventions are aligned closely with the Mission&apos;s Development Objective to ensure effective public service delivery under its current Country Development and Cooperation Strategy and to address Agency Climate Change policy priorities. Finally, INARA will maximize community engagement and incentives for reducing unnecessary energy consumption within selected municipalities while creating solid partnerships with the Lebanese diaspora that act as assistance multipliers.</narrative>
  </description>
